<?nvs
// The coherent tier over a Unix domain socket: the same two members as
// `examples/cache.nvs`, against a store `examples/cache-shared-socket.toml`
// reaches at a path instead of at an address.
//
// [ADR 0142](/docs/decisions/0142.md) is why this is
// a spelling in the operator's file and nothing in the program: the grant is
// `cache.shared`, which names the *store* and asks no address, so a store that
// has no address at all is not a special case of it. Nothing below mentions the
// transport, and that is the claim — a program written against the shared tier
// is already written against both.
//
// A build with no `AF_UNIX` transport refuses that URL at boot rather than
// reading it as loopback TCP, so this fixture is run only where there is one
// (its check in a goal record under `data/goals/` has `"needs": "af-unix"`). Printing
// "across the socket" over TCP is exactly what
// `rule:config/a-unix-spelling-with-no-af-unix-transport-refuses-at-boot`
// exists to prevent.
//
// The two lines this prints are frozen by an exact check in a goal record
// under `data/goals/`; the source is not.

var $shared = Core\Cache::shared();

// Out of the request heap and back into it, across a socket rather than a
// port. The value is compared rather than the absence, because "the store
// answered" is the weaker half of what a round trip proves.
$shared->put('socket-greeting', 'hello');
var $seen = $shared->get('socket-greeting');
if ($seen == 'hello') {
    echo 'put and get agree across the socket', "\n";
} else {
    echo 'the store did not answer with what it was given', "\n";
}

// The limiter, which opens no store of its own: `Core\RateLimit::consume` takes
// no address and asks the same `cache.shared` grant, so on this core it is the
// connection above that carries it — one socket per core, which is
// `nvs_stdlib::cache::redis`'s module doc. What a program can see from here is
// that both members reached the store this file configured and neither asked
// for anywhere else; that they share the *connection* is
// `the_limiter_and_the_tier_ask_one_grant_at_one_door` in
// `crates/nvs-stdlib/src/cache.rs`, which can see the door itself.
//
// The key is drawn rather than written down for `examples/cache.nvs`'s reason:
// the shared store does not forget when this process exits, and the sweep runs
// this program more than once.
var $account = 'socket-account:' . Core\Random::token(6);
var $first = Core\RateLimit::consume($account, 1, 2s);
if ($first->allowed()) {
    echo 'the limiter and the tier share one connection', "\n";
} else {
    echo 'the limiter refused a first arrival', "\n";
}
